1 OCCU Préposé général de la Nation juive en Alsace, représentant de la "nation juive" d'Alsace de 1764 à 1788, entrepreneur des fourrages pour les quatre provinces du Nord
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} 
2 CONT [http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herz_Cerfbeer_of_Medelsheim  Herz Cerfbeer] of Medelsheim (German: Herz Cerf Beer von Medelsheim, born Yiddish: נַפְתָּלִי(־הערץ) בֶּן דּוֹב־בּער Naphtali Ben Dov-Beer, born 1730, Medelsheim, or Bisch
2 CONC heim, Alsace - December 7, 1793, Strasbourg) was a French Jewish philanthropist. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Cerf Beer was a contractor to the army, and employed his wealth and his influence with the French government in promoting the material and spiritual welfare of his coreligionists. The government permitted him to settle at Strasbur
2 CONC g, in opposition to the wishes of the authorities of that city, who zealously enforced the law excluding Jews. He protected all Jews who were willing to earn a livelihood by manual labor. 
2 CONT
2 CONT As soon as he had received (in 1775) from Louis XVI the patent granting him the rights of citizenship "for services rendered by him to the government and to the land during the famine of 1770 and 1771," Cerfbeer established factor
2 CONC ies, where he employed Jews, in order to withdraw them from petty trading, and also to deprive their accusers of all excuse for prejudice.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Strasbourg Germans, who made every effort to prevent the Jews from settling in that city, compelled Cerfbeer to endeavor to obtain from the government the repeal of exceptional laws. A petition to the king was drawn up by Cerf
2 CONC beer and sent to Moses Mendelssohn for revision. The latter consulted Christian Wilhelm von Dohm, who offered to write an apology for the Jews. 
2 CONT
2 CONT This apology, Über die Bürgerliche Verbesserung der Juden, which Cerfbeer energetically spread in France, combined with his personal efforts, brought about the convocation by Malesherbes of a commission to make suggestions for the
2 CONC  amelioration of the condition of the Jews in France. Cerfbeer was the leading member of this commission; and the first result of its efforts was the abrogation of the degrading poll-tax.
2 CONT
2 CONT At the outbreak of the Reign of Terror in France, Cerfbeer was thrown into prison on suspicion of favoring the royal cause, but was set free after a year of confinement.
2 CONT
2 CONT Being acquainted with the Talmud, Cerfbeer took a great interest in Jewish literature. He supported a yeshiva at Bischheim and published at his own expense rare Hebrew books, among which was the Lechem Setarim of Solomon Nissim Al
2 CONC gazi. Wessely wrote a poem in honor of Cerfbeer (in Ha-Meassef, 1786, p. 49), and Abraham Auerbach dedicated to him his poem "Dibre ha-Mekes we-Bittulo."
2 CONT
2 CONT >>>><nowiki>-------------------------------------</nowiki>
2 CONT
2 CONT Cerf Beer (yiddish : נַפְתָּלִי־הערץ בֶּן דּוֹב־בּער Naftali Hertz ben Dov Beer) est un homme politique et un philanthrope juif alsacien du xviiie siècle (Medelsheim, 1726 – Strasbourg, 1793).
2 CONT « Préposé général 1 de la nation juive » d'Alsace, il est à ce titre l'un des grands acteurs de l'émancipation des Juifs de France.
2 CONT
2 CONT Wikipédia http://goo.gl/mayd1
2 CONT
2 CONT CERF BERR ET SON ÉPOQUE par M. Ginsburger PUBLICATION DE LA SOCIÉTÉ D'HISTOIRE DES JUIFS D'ALSACE-LORRAINE CONFÉRENCE faite à Strasbourg le 17 janvier 1906 http://goo.gl/MlxIe
2 CONT
2 CONT ------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Hirtz de Medelsheim dit Cerf Berr, ou Hirtz de Bischheim
2 CONT
2 CONT il a 8 enfants avec Jüdel (4 fils et 4 filles), puis se remarie à la mort de Jüdel avec Hana, qui avait 3 enfants
2 CONT
2 CONT http://judaisme.sdv.fr//perso/cerfberr/index.htm
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herz_Cerfbeer_of_Medelsheim
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT known as Hirz of Medelsheim (Alsace) he was army purveyor to the courts of King Louis XV and Louis XVI.  Immensely wealthy, he became a parnass of the Jewish community. His sons were to become influential members of the community,
2 CONC  Theodore, Lippmann and Baruch sitting with the Grand Sanhedrin of 1806 at Napoleon's request.
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT died 20/09/1794 ???
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
