1 OCCU négociant en fourrages, représentant des Juifs d'Alsace aux Etats généraux en 1789, membre de l'Assemblée des Notables et du Grand Sanhédrin (1806-1807)
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} *Membre du Grand Sanhédrin de Napoléon.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Théodore's Father:  Cerf Berr'''
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://jewishencyclopedia.com/articles/2693-beaugency '''Cerf-Berr'''], an Alsatian Jew, Théodore's father, rendered great service to the French government as purveyor to the army, was the interpreter of the Jews before Louis XVl
2 CONC .  The humane minister Malesherbes summoned a commission of jewish notables to make suggestions for the amelioration of the condition of their co-religionists.  This commission included Théodore's father, Cerf Berr , and eminent r
2 CONC epresentatives of the Portuguese Jews of Bordeaux and Bayonne, like Furtado, Gradis, Isaac Rodrigues, Lopez Dubec, etc.
2 CONT
2 CONT The direct result of the efforts of these men was the abolition, in 1784, of the degrading poll-tax and the permission to settle in all parts of France.
2 CONT
2 CONT mariage à Strasbourg selon ML
