1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abraham Weill's wife was a deeply religious woman who was horrified at her son's lack of religion.  Although she did not live with Bernard and Selma Weil after their marriage, she did live in Paris until her death 
2 CONC in the 1930s. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Having her living close by certainly made problems for the Weil family since when she visited her son and daughter-in-law, much to her horror, they prepared food for her which was not kosher.
