1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Please respect the following==
2 CONT =====Encyclopedia Titanica - https://www.encyclopedia-titanica.org/copyright-and-permissions.html '' "Simply because the information is displayed on this web site does not mean it is in the public domain or free to copy, publish o
2 CONC r distribute. Much of the material on this site is subject to applicable laws of copyright. You are more than welcome to link to any page on Encyclopedia Titanica but please do not copy pages or images" ''.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''See''' Encyclopedia Titanica (2018) Edgar Joseph Meyer (ref: #205, last updated: 23rd October 2018, accessed 25th September 2023 09:24:01 AM)
2 CONT URL : https://www.encyclopedia-titanica.org/titanic-victim/edgar-meyer.html
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Titanic Passenger Summary===
2 CONT
2 CONT Name: Mr Edgar Joseph Meyer
2 CONT Titanic Victim
2 CONT Born: Sunday 13th January 1884 in San Francisco, California, United States 
2 CONT Age: 28 years 3 months and 2 days (Male)
2 CONT Nationality: American
2 CONT Marital Status: Married to Leila Saks
2 CONT Last Residence: in New York City, New York, United States
2 CONT Occupation: Mechanical Engineer
2 CONT 1st Class Passengers
2 CONT Embarked: Cherbourg on Wednesday 10th April 1912
2 CONT Ticket No. 17604, £82 3s 5d 
2 CONT Died in the Titanic disaster (15th April 1912)
2 CONT Body Not Identified
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [http://person.ancestry.com/tree/89854924/person/78004067979 Ancestry Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 30 2016, 5:03:30 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT The youngest child of Eugene Meyer and his wife. He has seven siblings in all. He was 28 years old in 1912 and had been married for 2½ years. He and his wife had a year-old daughter. Meyer was a graduate of Cornell University, whe
2 CONC re he took his degree as a Mechanical Engineer. His discovery of a method to measure the velocity of flame propagation in gasoline engines became a standard technique. After his graduation from college he joined his brother in bus
2 CONC iness in Wall Street and became vice president of the Braden Copper Company of NYC. A resident of New York City, Mr Meyer boarded the Titanic at Cherbourg as a first class passenger (PC 17604, £82 3s 5d) together with his wife Lei
2 CONC la Meyer. Meyer was described as having a gentle and pleasing personality as well as a manly, straightforward manner. Mr Meyer perished in the disaster. His body, if recovered, was never identified.
2 CONT * Reference: [http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&amp;GRid=53394683 Find A Grave Memorial] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Mar 30 2016, 5:23:54 UTC''
