1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Abraham Weil, a prominent member of the Jewish community in Alsace, perhaps a Dayan as he was called in to adujicate disputes in the community.  His wife was a deeply religious woman who was horrified at her son, B
2 CONC ernhard's lack of religion. 
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham a épousé la soeur cadette de sa première épouse, au décès de celle-ci, et ils ont eu deux fils, Bernard et Oscar.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jusqu'en 1918, Weill s'écrit avec 2 "l" (orthographe alsacienne), ce n'est plus le cas à la génération suivante
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham quitte Wolfisheim pour Strasbourg vers 1857, il est marchand de biens
2 CONT
2 CONT [http://books.google.com/books?id=OdeDlT9-GBUC&lpg=PA77&ots=p9Awk3oarT&dq=ancestry%20Simone%20Weil&pg=PA87#v=onepage&q=ancestry%20Simone%20Weil&f=false At Home with Antoine and Simone Weil] gives Abraham's parents names as Benjami
2 CONC n Weill and Ghina Gross.
2 CONT
2 CONT ---------
