1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Sophie and Theodore were married in a house on Sutter street.  A type of ballroom was built on an empty lot next to the house especially for the wedding.
2 CONT
2 CONT Below is a description of the photographs and letters in the Magnes Collection:
2 CONT
2 CONT Sophie Gerstle Lilienthal was the daughter of Lewis (Lob) Gerstle and Hannah (Johannah) Greenebaum, of San Francisco. On 27 Aug. 1879, she married Theodore Max Lilienthal. Lilienthal was the director of Lilienthal Brothers, hops a
2 CONC nd grain, of New York.
2 CONT
2 CONT The collection contains a photograph album holding photographs of many prominent Jewish families, It also contains two hundred and fifty-two letters that Theodore sent to and received from Sophie and eight others that he sent to a
2 CONC nd received from other members of his family and his personal friends. Theodore's letters to Sophie illuminate his deep love and devotion to her, and his beliefs that a woman's place in society and within her own marriage should b
2 CONC e determined by her husband and that a wife should practice frugality and order. Also contains a menu from Theodore and Sophie's wedding, as well as a bill from San Francisco's Palace Hotel. Besides containing many poems that Theo
2 CONC dore wrote to and gave to Sophie, it also has one poem that he sent to his father, Rabbi Max Lilienthal, in 1880, on the occasion of Max's twenty-fifth jubilee as rabbi of Cincinnati's Congregation Bene Israel.
2 CONT
