1 OCCU prêtre, vicaire de la cathédrale de Strasbourg, founder of the Congregation of Notre-Dame de Sion
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} fondateur de la Congrégation de Notre Dame de Sion (1842)
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Theodore Ratisbonne. converted to Christianity in 1827 and became a Priest at the end of  1830. At 1840 he came to live in Paris. He founded the congregation for Nuns Of Notre Dame de Sion (The "Sisters of Sion") and later 
2 CONC - "The Sion Fathers". His younger brother, Alphonse "Marie", Converted to Christianity on 1842 and became a Priest too. Later he joined his elder brother in management of the congregations and at 1855  he arrived in Jerusalem (The
2 CONC  Holy Land) and was responsible for the building of 3 Monasteries  for the congregations. (See his profile). 
2 CONT
2 CONT See the Site: http://www.notredamedesion.org/en/page.php?id=3&T=1 [Added by Michael D. Bruell]
