1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A scholar, author and collector, died on September 24, 1997. He was 87 years old. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Liebman attended Harvard College and subsequently moved to Paris to study at the Ecole des Hautes Etudes. He received his diploma after submitting a thesis entitled ''La Vie Prose de St. Denys''. Mr. Liebman's publications inc
2 CONC lude numerous articles on medieval literature and a book regarding the life of Simon de Tournai. He was often consulted by the Morgan Library to assist in the identification of manuscripts in its possession. He collected rare maps
2 CONC  of Paris, which he exhibited at the Grolier Club, of which he was a member. 
2 CONT
2 CONT Mr. Liebman is survived by his loving sister, Margaret L. Berger and brother-inlaw, Adolph R. Berger, M.D.
