2 CONT
2 CONT Rabbi Hemmerdinger studied under his father-in-law, R. Aron BLUEM (Blum) in Bollwiller (H-R), in accordance with his marriage contract, and served as his assistant.  In 1784 he was the Rabbi in Blotzheim (H-R).  In 1796 he was app
2 CONC ointed by the the Rabbinic Chair in Bollwiller, which had jurisdiction in Baden, to be Oberrabbiner in Baden.  There was dispute, however, with the son of the previous rabbi, then deceased, as a result R. Hemmerdinger was appointe
2 CONC d to the seat in Eichstetten, instead.
1 NOTE I can tell you that I am also a GUGGENHEIM in three
2 CONT different ways. The most important is through my 5x
2 CONT great grandmother, Elle bat Samuel Gougenheim, of
2 CONT Scherwiller, Alsace #49 on your p. 93 who was married
2 CONT to Rabbi Aron Hemmerdinger. I have a vast family tree
2 CONT of all of their descendants, more 4000!
2 CONT
2 CONT The  gr-gr grandson of Elle and Aron, a grandson of
2 CONT Morenu HaRav Joseph H. whose circumcision record I
2 CONT found in the Mohelbuch of Dambach.   His name
2 CONT was(Chaim Loeb) Leopold Hemmerdinger,  son of Rabbi
2 CONT Marx H.  Leopold was born in Blotzheim,  but  was
2 CONT living in Eichstetten, Germany, where his father had
2 CONT been sent to be the rabbi.  Leopold married Dusette
2 CONT Guggenheim, of Lengau, daughter of Meyer G. and his
2 CONT wife Vogele.  These were my great-great grandparents.
2 CONT
2 CONT After the death of Dusette, Leopold then married her
2 CONT niece, Clara Bernheim of Lengnau, the daughter of
2 CONT Dusette's sister Pess (Babette).
