1 NOTE [hemmerdinger.FTW]
2 CONT
2 CONT Information on marriage of  Emmanuel and Sarle from:
2 CONT
2 CONT Fraenckel - P. 202l
2 CONT
2 CONT Emmanuel chose name in 1808 in Haguenau. His wife at that time is shown as Judith Lévy.  A daughter, Flore Mimi is also listed, but it is not possible to determine who was her mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT At time of marriage to Sarle he was named as:
2 CONT Menahem-Zevy (Menke-Hirsch) son of Rabbi Mosche (Kochel) of Marmoutier.
2 CONT Moche (Kochel) was presumably the same as "Kostel", married to Merle Levy in  Marmoutier in 1748 (Fraenckel - P. 109 j)j
2 CONT
2 CONT Menke is listed in 1784 as "beau-fils (stepson)  in Family #20, Hagenau.
