2 CONC olume Landesarchiv Baden-Württemberg - Staatsarchiv Freiburg L10 Bd. 0468, Breisach am Rhein, Breisach, Baden, Germany, Landesarchiv Baden-Württemberg, Freiburg, Deutschland (Baden-Württemberg Provincial Archives, Freiburg, German
2 CONC y). "Germany, Baden, Church Book Duplicates, 1800-1870," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.1.1/2D9Y-NJ6 : accessed 2 March 2016), Alexander Nieheim in entry for Wolf Kahn Greilsamer and Jeanette Nieheim, 04
2 CONC  Mar 1846; citing p. 39, volume Landesarchiv Baden-Württemberg - Staatsarchiv Freiburg L10 Bd. 0468, Breisach am Rhein, Breisach, Baden, Germany, Landesarchiv Baden-Württemberg, Freiburg, Deutschland (Baden-Württemberg Provincial 
2 CONC Archives, Freiburg, Germany).
2 CONT
2 CONT David Blum said the family name Nieheim had been Salomon before 1809 and that he was called Alexander Salomon-this was mentioned in the death certificate.
2 CONT
2 CONT 20 Jul 1808. Decree concerning the Jews without fixed surnames and forenames.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art. 1: Those of the subjects of our Empire who follow the Hebraic worship and who until now, do not have fixed family names and forenames, will be required to adopt such names within the next three months of the publication o
2 CONC f our present decree and to make statement in front of the local civil officer where they are domiciled.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art 2: The foreign Jews who would come to live in the Empire and that would be in cases mentioned in Art.1 will be required to follow the same formality within three months following their admission in France.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art.3: Surnames that are not permitted: no name drawn from the Old Testament and no city name. As forenames those allowed by law of 11 germinal Year 11 will be able to be taken.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art 4: The consistories in making the list of the Jews of their communities will be obliged to give proof...
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art.5: The Jews of our states or foreign Jews, who would come to settle, will be exempted from the conditions of our present decree, when they will have known surname and first name or when they always have been carrying the a
2 CONC forementioned names and forenames even though they are drawn from the Old Testament or from cities, where they had been living.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art.6: Jews mentioned in the previous article and who will want to keep their names and forenames, will however be required to make known the declaration: the Jews of our states in the town-hall of the place where they are dom
2 CONC iciled, and the foreign Jews in the town-hall of where they plan to settle; the whole within the time frame stipulated in the article 1.
2 CONT
2 CONT     Art.7: Contains sanctions.
2 CONT
2 CONT     (Galisset: Corps du droit français (August, 1801 - March, 1814)) 
2 CONT
2 CONT Juden in Breisach by Hans David Blum   ISBN 3-89649-362-0
2 CONT
2 CONT This book is in the library of the Leo Baeck Institute in NY.
2 CONT
2 CONT Page 215 - In list of names adopted by Jews of Breisach:
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander Salomon became Alexander Salomon NIEHEIM. He was 37 in 1809. His wife
2 CONT
2 CONT was Sara, age 33.  Children: Ella, 13; Helene, 8;  Schoena, 7; Veyele, 1 1/2
2 CONT
2 CONT and Jakob, 2.
2 CONT
2 CONT in a document about Rosina he was a "Handelsman"
2 CONT
2 CONT "Alexander I found listed as a boy in Alsace (1784) with his siblings and widowed STEPMOTHER.  She married in 1797 Wolf Mock in Breisach"
2 CONT
2 CONT Many family details about the interconnected Salomon family whose seat was in a town across the Rhine (Parnas Family)"
2 CONT
2 CONT Alexander's stepmother became later his Aunt, Herz Mock was an older cousin, whose daughter became Alexander's wife."
2 CONT
2 CONT "Germany, Baden, Church Book Duplicates, 1800-1870," database, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/pal:/MM9.1.1/2D9Y-JQV : accessed 9 February 2016), Alexander Nieheim in entry for Joseph Weishaupt and Fanny Nieheim, 09 Aug 184
2 CONC 1; citing p. 64, volume Landesarchiv Baden-Württemberg - Staatsarchiv Freiburg L10 Bd. 0468, Breisach am Rhein, Breisach, Baden, Germany, Landesarchiv Baden-Württemberg, Freiburg, Deutschland (Baden-Württemberg Provincial Archives
2 CONC , Freiburg, Germany). The image is viewable at www2.landesarchiv-bw.de.
