1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Leon was a key organizer in the 1915 San Francisco Pan Pacific Exposition, an important event after the devastation of the 1906 earthquake, according to Irene Narell, author of _Our City, the Jews of San Francisco.
2 CONC  He is listed as owning 125 shares of stock  in the San Francisco and San Joaquin Valley Railway Company, according to Pioneers of Prosperity by David H. Walker, San Francisco, 1895. Pages 121-136, Submitted by: Nancy Pratt Melton
2 CONC , in http://freepages.genealogy.rootsweb.com/~npmelton/RAIL.htm
2 CONT
2 CONT Louis was appointed by Leland Stanford to Stanford's first Board of Trustees in 1891, according to the Lowell High School Alumni Association,  http://www.lowellalumni.org/history_19century.shtml
