1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ===Individual Note===
2 CONT BOWEN Evelyn W., passed away peacefully April 28, 2002 after a long bout with cancer. Born in New York City, December 29, 1911, daughter of Minnie and Felix WILDENSTEIN, founder of the American branch of the Wildenstein Galleries 
2 CONC in New York City. Resident of Fort Lauderdale since 1954, pre-deceased by her husband, Stephen, a Founder and First President and President Emeritus of the Fort Lauderdale Museum of Art. Mrs. BOWEN was a long-time member of the Ho
2 CONC ly Gross Hospital Auxiliary, charter member of Beaux Arts and former Publicity Chairperson of the Fort Lauderdale Symphony Society. She is survived by a large and loving family: sister, Andree Dormeuil, Paris, France; daughter, Ma
2 CONC ry-Jane Graff, Fort Lauderdale; sons, Michael BOWEN, Palm Beach and Martin BOWEN, Charleston, SC; grandchildren: Stephen, Lisa, Warren, Michelle, Bryan, David, Douglas and Christopher; great grandchildren: Ashley, Welsh, Kelley, M
2 CONC egan, Madeline, Leo and Taylor. Visitation Tuesday, April 30th, 5:00 to 8:00 PM in the funeral home. Funeral Mass Wednesday, May 1st, 11:30 AM at St. Sebastian Catholic Church. In lieu of flowers, donations to St. Sebastian Cathol
2 CONC ic Church, 2000 S.E. 25th Avenue, Fort Lauderdale 33316. Baird-Case/Jordan-Fannin Funeral Home, 4343 N. Federal Highway,  http://www.legacy.com/obituaries/sunsentinel/obituary.aspx?n=evelyn-w-bowen&pid=312957* Reference: [https://
2 CONC gw.geneanet.org/vparmentier3?lang=en&pz=veronique&nz=parmentier&p=evelyn&n=wildenstein Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Oct 9 2019, 13:20:08 UTC''
