1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://www.findagrave.com/cgi-bin/fg.cgi?page=gr&GSln=+Schuster&GSfn=George+&GSmn=Ernest+&GSby=1881&GSbyrel=in&GSdy=1982&GSdyrel=in&GSob=n&GRid=94643768&df=all&
2 CONT
2 CONT Birth: 	Apr. 25, 1881 Death: 	Jun. 5, 1982, England
2 CONT
2 CONT Sir George Ernest Schuster, KCSI, KCMG, CBE, MC was a British barrister, financier, colonial administrator and Liberal politician. Son of Ernest and Hilda Schuster  At the outbreak of the First World War, Schuster was working in f
2 CONC inance in the City of London, and was prospective Liberal parliamentary candidate for North Cumberland. He held a commission in the Oxfordshire Yeomanry, and was mobilised to serve on the Western Front until 1918, when he joined t
2 CONC he allied force in the Murmansk area. He ended the war with the rank of lieutenant-colonel, having been awarded the Military Cross and appointed Commander of the Order of the British Empire. He was also decorated with the Russian 
2 CONC Order of St. Vladimir. His is brother Lt Alfred Schuster and son Captain Richard Douglas Schuster were killed in WWI. Sir George Schuster died aged 101 
2 CONT
2 CONT Burial: Nether Worton St James Churchyard  Nether Worton West Oxfordshire District Oxfordshire, England
