2 CONT Another son, Herbert James Baumann, graduated from Grey College and studied engineering in Germany. He farmed in Winburg, then worked as a clerk in Smaldeel (later known as Theunissen), and managed Wolf Ehrlich’s farm in Ladybrand
2 CONC .22 A veld-cornet, he fought at the Siege of Kimberley and the Battle of Magersfontein and, as a prisoner of war, was sent to St. Helena. He came back almost blind. 
2 CONT ----
