1 NOTE {geni:about_me} n 1880 Helene, third daughter of Caroline and Isaac Baumann, was married in Bloemfontein by the Reverend Rappaport to Wolf Ehrlich, a businessman, originally from Erfurt, Germany. Ehrlich opened the first shoe shop
2 CONC  in Bloemfontein and was a founder of the Bloemfontein Chamber of Commerce. A Member of Parliament in the Orange River Colony, and Senator for the Orange Free State, he was also a three term mayor of Bloemfontein, and for a while,
2 CONC  the Portuguese Consul! He helped found the South African Jewish Board of Deputies and was the first President of the Bloemfontein Hebrew Congregation. Helene was a suffragette, and active in the Jewish Women’s Benevolent Society.
2 CONC  The Ehrlichs had nine children: Theresa, Minnie, Rosalie, Julian, Hedwig, Henry, Carl Otto, Gladys and Caroline. Rosalie was a well- known theater producer, suffragette and founding member of the South African Communist Party. Sh
2 CONC e won the British Empire Shakespeare Competition and founded the first Afrikaans Eisteddfod. She too wrote her memoir
2 CONT
2 CONT South Africa, Orange Free State, Probate Records from the Master of the Supreme Court,  Helene Baumann Ehrlich birth:1860 Bloemfontein death:9 September 1934 probate 1934 Pretoria,South Africa Six children are listed. Julian Isaac
2 CONC  Baumann Ehrlich; Rosalie Isolde Ehrlich; Hedwig Hannah Harris (born Ehrlich); Carl Otto Ehrlich; Gladys Ella van Hees (born Ehrlich); Tessa Caroline Ehrlich.
