2 CONC ng enumeration district (ED) ED 861, sheet 11B, line 79, family 299, NARA microfilm publication T626 (Washington D.C.: National Archives and Records Administration, 2002), roll 1538; FHL microfilm 2,341,273. 
2 CONT
2 CONT "United States World War II Draft Registration Cards, 1942," database with images, FamilySearch (https://familysearch.org/ark:/61903/1:1:F3CY-6ZS : 7 April 2016), Rudolf Church, 1942; citing NARA microfilm publication M1936, M1937
2 CONC , M1939, M1951, M1962, M1964, M1986, M2090, and M2097 (Washington D.C.: National Archives and Records Administration, n.d.).
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT CARE
2 CONT The Bundesarchiv Gedenkbuch looks likely to have "confused" the KIRCHBERGER born 1893 with this one born 1900 in Wien (who died in Wien 21 June 1944, according to the web page):
2 CONT https://rudolf-kirchberger.zurerinnerung.at/
2 CONT
2 CONT The KIRCHBERGER born 1893 is quite likely to be related to these KIRCHBERGERs from Niederlahnstein:
2 CONT https://archive.org/details/hellmannkirchber1351unse/page/n93/mode/...
2 CONT
2 CONT Searched Yad Vashem:  no entry.
2 CONT ----
2 CONT ''Bundesarchiv Gedenkbuch:''
