1 CONT Benjamin and Schonele lived in Jungholtz, Alsace at the time oftheir  marriage.  She was the daughter of Leopold (Jehuda Leibben Josel s'l')  Salomon of Biescheim and Ella bas Meir Netter.Benjamin ben Joseph ben  Aron of Scherwill
1 CONC er had his brotherEisik mentioned as given rights to  "Chaliza" in his marriagecontract.  The bride brought a dowry of 3,000  Reichsthaler. Theyoung couple had the right to eat for four years "amFamilientisch."  The bride was assu
1 CONC red of receiving half of amale heir.  In Nov., 1784, Benjamin was listed in the census ofJews of Alsace as the  Rabbi in Niedernheim (Niedernai).  Theinformation on his second wife and  children is taken from thatdocument and also
1 CONC  from a letter of Pierre  Lautmann, Nov., 1995.
1 CONT
1 CONT Benjamin is buried in the Jewish cemetery of Rosenwiller,Section III,  grave 10.  The inscription reads: "Rabbi BenjaminHemmerdinger,  Rabbin  du Territoire de la Noblesse Immediate deBasse Alsace a Niedernai, 1771  a 1783."  Info
1 CONC rmation on thisgravesite from a letter of Robert Veil of  Versaille, 28 Nov.,1988.  Additional information from Raphael & Weyl's  book,"Regards Nouveau sur les Juifs d'Alsace."  Rosanne and DanielLeeson visited this grave in the s
1 CONC ummer of 1995 and photographedit.  A  photo may also be found in the book "Le Cemetiere Juifde Rosenwiller" of  Robert Wey.
0 @N6000000002764987417@ NOTE
